# oxfmt formats non-code files (YAML / JSON / Markdown). Exclude files that are
# generated, vendored, or owned by another tool — reformatting them creates
# churn or breaks downstream tooling.
#
# CRITICAL: changelog files are owned by release-please / git-cliff. If oxfmt
# reformats them, the next regeneration conflicts and CI fmt-check falsely fails
# on every PR between releases. Always exclude them.

# Vendored / generated code
vendor/
*.pb.go

# Tool-owned changelogs — DO NOT reformat
changelog/
CHANGELOG.md
.release-please-manifest.json
release-please-config.json

# Lockfiles
**/buf.lock
Cargo.lock

# Build output
dist/
build/
bin/
target/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lockra
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependency and tool state (oxfmt reads this file instead of .gitignore).
node_modules/
coverage/
.codegraph/
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Generated by tauri-build (capability schemas).
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# Written by the Rust contract test in serde_json's own layout and compared byte
# for byte (crates/lockra-bridge/tests/contract.rs): never reformat.
**/fixtures/ipc/

# Other apps' exports as those apps write them, read by the import's tests.
crates/lockra-transfer/tests/fixtures/

# Third-party data, byte for byte as published and pinned by SHA-256
# (crates/lockra-autofill/data/SOURCES, scripts/update-vendored-data.sh).
crates/lockra-autofill/data/

# The browser extension's contract vectors, written by crates/lockra-browser/tests/protocol.rs
# and compared byte for byte.
crates/lockra-browser/tests/vectors/
